---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Architecture — CareLoop';
const description =
  'CareLoop data flow: capture, two-pass grounded extraction, encrypted per-household cells, the MCP Streamable-HTTP server, the dose-free policy guard and the two surfaces.';

// name -> one-line intent, from careloop/tools.py TOOL_DEFS
const tools = [
  ['about_careloop', 'Explain what CareLoop can do; the guest-safe entry point and first-run examples.'],
  ['get_care_plan', 'List what to do next for one person, pending items first, dose-masked on the voice surface.'],
  ['explain_instruction', 'Show the clinician’s original recorded sentence for one item and when it was recorded.'],
  ['mark_done', 'Record that one care item was completed (idempotent, with version conflict detection).'],
  ['confirm_instruction', 'Clear a flagged item’s “needs confirmation” flag after the caregiver checks with the clinician.'],
  ['add_note', 'Remember one short verbal instruction exactly as given; never adds medical advice.'],
  ['delete_instruction', 'Remove an item — reads it back first and requires explicit confirmation (destructive).'],
  ['list_people', 'List the people in this household’s care plans.'],
  ['todays_plan', 'Today’s agenda for one person, ordered by time of day.'],
  ['what_changed', 'Diff this visit against the previous one: new, stopped and changed items.'],
  ['prepare_next_visit', 'Build the caregiver’s question list from flagged, superseded and note items — no advice.'],
  ['daily_digest', 'How much of today’s plan is done versus pending.'],
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="cl-prose">
    <h1>Architecture</h1>
    <p class="u-mute">
      One self-hosted Python process speaks MCP over Streamable HTTP and serves both surfaces. The
      same outbound guard is applied to every response, which is what makes the voice surface
      dose-free by construction.
    </p>

    <h2>Data flow</h2>
    <pre class="cl-pre" aria-label="CareLoop data flow diagram"><code>  clinician's words
  (paste / upload / dictate)
            │
            ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────┐   crisis / child / injection   ┌─────────────┐
  │  policy_guard (inbound)  │ ───── rejects / redirects ───► │  stop line  │
  └──────────────────────────┘                                └─────────────┘
            │ transcript (treated as DATA, never instructions)
            ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────┐
  │  extract: two-pass       │
  │   1. rules extractor     │  deterministic, always runs
  │   2. Bedrock pass 1      │  pointer-only schema (no free text)
  │      Bedrock pass 2      │  verifier  ·  falls back to rules on error
  │   validate_pointers +    │
  │   quote_guard (verbatim) │  span must be inside its sentence AND in the transcript
  └──────────────────────────┘
            │ items &#123;kind, span, quote, schedule, confidence, needs_confirm&#125;
            ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────┐   transcript → SHA-256 hash only
  │  store: per-household    │   (raw transcript not kept by default)
  │  encrypted SQLite cell   │   AES-256-GCM fields · append-only hash-chained ledger
  │  + crypto-shred erasure  │
  └──────────────────────────┘
            │ structuredContent
            ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────┐   OAuth 2.1 + PKCE(S256) · PRM/AS metadata · MCP-Session-Id
  │  careloop.mcp_server     │ ◄── POST /mcp  (Streamable HTTP)
  │  /mcp  + companion API   │
  └──────────────────────────┘
        │                    │
        │ guard_payload      │ full doses (ViewDose, companion only)
        │ (mask_doses +      │
        │  disclaimer +      ▼
        │  attribution) ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────────┐
        └──────────────►│  Alexa voice  │        │ companion page     │
                        │  surface      │        │ (behind household  │
                        │  dose-free    │        │  login) — full dose│
                        └───────────────┘        └────────────────────┘
                                     ▲                      ▲
                              authz.decide  ── one decision point, Cedar-style,
                                              differentially tested vs policies.cedar</code></pre>

    <h2>MCP transport &amp; auth</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Streamable HTTP</strong> at <span class="cl-kbd">POST /mcp</span>; GET is refused
        with <span class="cl-kbd">405</span> (no server-initiated SSE stream). Batch requests are
        rejected; notifications get <span class="cl-kbd">202</span>.</li>
      <li><strong>MCP-Session-Id</strong> is issued on <span class="cl-kbd">initialize</span> and
        required on initialised requests; an unknown session returns <span class="cl-kbd">404</span>
        and a bad <span class="cl-kbd">MCP-Protocol-Version</span> header returns
        <span class="cl-kbd">400</span>.</li>
      <li><strong>OAuth 2.1</strong> authorization-code with <strong>PKCE (S256)</strong> only; static
        clients authenticate with a Basic header, and credentials in the query string are rejected.
        Tokens are audience-bound and expire.</li>
      <li><strong>PRM / AS metadata</strong> are served at
        <span class="cl-kbd">/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource</span> and
        <span class="cl-kbd">/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server</span>; unauthenticated calls
        return <span class="cl-kbd">401</span> with a <span class="cl-kbd">WWW-Authenticate</span>
        pointer to the resource metadata.</li>
      <li><strong>policy_guard</strong> is the last gate on every Alexa-surface response: dose
        masking, disclaimer and attribution, plus a residual dose-leak check that hard-sanitizes and
        counts.</li>
      <li><strong>Bedrock two-pass with rules fallback</strong>: pass 1 points into the transcript,
        pass 2 verifies; if the model is throttled or unreachable the pipeline degrades to the
        deterministic rules extractor rather than failing.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The twelve MCP tools</h2>
    <p>One intent per tool, validated inputs and declared output schemas:</p>
    <div class="cl-panel" style="padding-inline:0;overflow:hidden;margin-top:var(--cl-sp-4);">
      <table class="cl-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">CareLoop MCP tools and their intents</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">Intent</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {tools.map(([name, intent]) => (
            <tr><th scope="row"><span class="cl-kbd">{name}</span></th><td>{intent}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="cl-note" style="margin-top:var(--cl-sp-5);">
      Storage layout: <span class="cl-kbd">&lt;db_root&gt;/cells/&lt;sha16(hid)&gt;/care.db</span> per
      household, a separate keyring, and a global DB of households, links and tombstones that holds
      no PHI. See <a href="/docs/judging">the judging map</a> for the files behind each claim.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
